# docs.rules
version: 1

## MUST
- No broken relative links to files that don't exist in the repo.
- Code samples in documentation are syntactically valid for the language they claim to be.
- No secrets, API keys, or internal-only URLs/hostnames included as examples.

## SHOULD
- Behavior changes in `src/` are reflected in the relevant docs in the same PR (README, integration guide, etc.).

## SECURITY
- (No additional checks beyond the MUST items above — docs changes carry low inherent security risk.)
